runex carries this fix to Rune until upstream (github.com/anomalyco/rune) has one. Upstream's
dev branch is still without it at d12581bc (2026-11-07): crates/rune/src/gpu and rune-light are
unchanged there since d03349e2, and no branch calls setThreadgroupMemoryLength.

The bug. Rune's own Metal backend (the macOS default) never sets the length of a compute
pipeline's threadgroup arguments (setThreadgroupMemoryLength:atIndex:). naga makes each
var<workgroup> global an entry point uses one of those arguments, so the kernel gets 0 bytes.
rune-light's field pass (field.wgsl: local_ids, local_n) is the only built-in kernel with such
globals: on macOS its tiles see no occluders or emitters, so there are no soft shadows and no
GI, and god rays aren't masked. RUNE_GPU_BACKEND=wgpu, Linux and Windows are unaffected:
wgpu-hal sets them (metal/device.rs collects wg_memory_sizes, metal/command.rs sets each).

The fix. shader.rs translate() collects the size of each workgroup global the entry point
uses, in global order, as wgpu-hal does, and compute.rs sets each length, rounded up to 16
bytes, when a pass sets the pipeline. A precompiled built-in function (builtin_native.metallib)
has no naga IR at hand, and parsing its module is what precompiling saves. So its pipeline is
made with reflection (MTLPipelineOptionBindingInfo), which reports its threadgroup arguments,
and so is a passthrough metallib's (create_shader_module_passthrough), which wgpu-hal leaves
unset. Reflection adds about 0.1 ms to a pipeline's creation (measured on an M3) and leaves
builtin_table.rs and the metallibs as upstream generated them. compute_tests.rs checks a kernel
with a var<workgroup> array and an atomic against wgpu's.

To drop it: once upstream fixes this, delete this file and run `node scripts/prepare-rune.mjs
--reapply` (it rebuilds vendor/rune from the pin and the patches left, so the update's preflight
check passes), move vendor/rune to a revision with the fix (bun scripts/update-rune.ts <rev>),
and check that `light verify` (cargo run --release -p
rune-light --example light -- verify) gives max |gpu - cpu| = 0.0226 on the default backend.

